\]

##### Decision Variables

For each $i \in S$, $j \in D$:
\[
x_{ij} \geq 0
\]
Quantity shipped from supplier $i$ to customer group $j$ (continuous).

##### Objective

\[
\min \sum_{i \in S} \sum_{j \in D} c_{ij} x_{ij}
\]

##### Constraints

1. **Demand satisfaction** (each customer group receives at least its demand):
   \[
   \sum_{i \in S} x_{ij} \geq d_j \qquad \forall j \in D
   \]

2. **Supply capacity** (each supplier does not exceed its capacity):
   \[
   \sum_{j \in D} x_{ij} \leq s_i \qquad \forall i \in S
   \]

3. **Non-negativity**:
   \[
   x_{ij} \geq 0 \qquad \forall i \in S,\, j \in D
   \]

##### Full Numerical Model

Let $S = \{\text{supply1}, \text{supply2}, \text{supply3}, \text{supply4}, \text{supply5}, \text{supply6}, \text{supply7}, \text{supply8}\}$, $D = \{\text{demand1}, \text{demand2}, \text{demand3}, \text{demand4}, \text{demand5}, \text{demand6}, \text{demand7}, \text{demand8}\}$.

\[
\begin{align*}
\min\ & \sum_{i \in S} \sum_{j \in D} c_{ij} x_{ij} \\
\text{s.t.}\quad
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand1}} \geq 9 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand2}} \geq 66 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand3}} \geq 56 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand4}} \geq 17 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand5}} \geq 43 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand6}} \geq 62 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand7}} \geq 10 \\
& \sum_{i \in S} x_{i,\text{demand8}} \geq 37 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply1},j} \leq 60 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply2},j} \leq 22 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply3},j} \leq 16 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply4},j} \leq 14 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply5},j} \leq 19 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply6},j} \leq 70 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply7},j} \leq 60 \\
& \sum_{j \in D} x_{\text{supply8},j} \leq 39 \\
& x_{ij} \geq 0 \qquad \forall i \in S,\, j \in D
\end{align*}
\]
where $c_{ij}$ are as given in the cost table above.[0m

